==Tagalog==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|G.I.}}

===Etymology===
Initialism originally from {{bor|tl|en|GI|t=nickname for [[USA|U.S.]] military personnel}}. The words to the {{initialism|tl||nocap=1}} was later jokingly perceived as {{m|en|"[[genuine#English|'''G'''enuine]] [[Intsik#Tagalog|'''I'''ntsik]]"}}, from {{compound|en|genuine|lang1=en|Intsik|t2=[[Chinese]]|lang2=tl|nocat=1}}.

===Noun===
{{tl-noun}}

# {{lb|tl|Chinese Filipino|humorous|slang}} {{initialism of|tl|[[genuine#English|Genuine]] [[Intsik#Tagalog|Intsik]]|nodot=1}} ([[Chinese]]) {{q|a term referring to any [[ethnic]] [[Chinese]] person in the [[Philippines]] described to be profoundly [[Chinese]] in [[behavior]], [[speech]], [[demeanor]], or [[likeness]], especially those [[born]] and [[raise]]d in [[China]] or [[Taiwan]].}}
#: ''Ang lalim ng Chinese (vocabulary) ng '''GI''' na nakilala ko, at di kami nagkaintindihan kahit sabay kaming gumagamit ng Mandarin.''
#:: The Chinese (vocabulary), used by the '''GI''' I met, was quite deep, and we couldn't understand each other even though we were both using Mandarin.

